  },
  "key_facts": [
    {
      "fact": "The official MCP registry held 24,477 servers with a latest version on 2026-08-24: 24,220 active and 257 deprecated, a net gain of 2,360 over the 2026-08-17 sweep (2,388 appeared, 28 disappeared)",
      "source": "jsonhouse original measurement, 2026-08-24",
      "category": "data"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Of the top 100 servers by GitHub stars, 75 have a namespace matching the repository owner, 4 do not, and 21 use domain namespaces that cannot be checked mechanically",
      "source": "jsonhouse original measurement, 2026-08-24",
      "category": "data"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The rank-4 entry io.github.IncorporatedPartners/labelhead-artist-momentum, a hip-hop analytics server, declares the unrelated repository paperclipai/paperclip and inherits its 79,252 stars, 654 of which it gained in the week to 2026-08-24",
      "source": "jsonhouse original measurement, 2026-08-24",
      "category": "case_study"
    },
    {
      "fact": "65 of the top 100 servers by stars declare a repository that is not dedicated to the MCP server (repository name lacks 'mcp'); their median star count is 6,562 versus 4,334 for the 35 dedicated repositories",
      "source": "jsonhouse original measurement, 2026-08-24",
      "category": "data"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The registry publishes no first-registration timestamp: its publishedAt field tracks the latest version, so 583 servers present in both the 2026-08-17 and 2026-08-24 sweeps moved to a different month without being new, and counts for past months decay as servers republish",
      "source": "jsonhouse original measurement, roster comparison 2026-08-17 to 2026-08-24",
      "category": "definition"
    },
    {
      "fact": "2,630 of 19,049 declared repositories (13.8%) returned no public response when queried",
      "source": "jsonhouse original measurement, 2026-08-24",
      "category": "data"
    },
    {
      "fact": "5,428 servers (22.2% of the registry) declare no repository at all and cannot appear in any star-based ranking",
      "source": "jsonhouse original measurement, 2026-08-24",
      "category": "data"
    },
    {
      "fact": "A single namespace, io.github.pipeworx-io, holds 1,312 servers — 5.36% of the registry; the top ten hold 16.06%, up from 12.44% a week earlier after io.github.mcp-dir grew from 236 servers to 1,095",
      "source": "jsonhouse original measurement, 2026-08-24",
      "category": "trend"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The MCP registry verifies namespace ownership via GitHub OAuth or a DNS TXT record but does not verify the repository URL; the publishing token requires no repository scopes because the registry never reads publisher code",
      "source": "MCP Registry authentication documentation, retrieved 2026-08-24",
      "category": "policy"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The registry's moderation policy states that it does not guarantee moderation, that consumers should assume minimal-to-no moderation, and that consumers should treat scraped data accordingly",
      "source": "MCP Registry moderation policy, retrieved 2026-08-24",
      "category": "policy"
    }
  ],
  "faq_summary": [
    {
      "q": "How many MCP servers exist in the official registry?",
      "a": "24,477 servers had a latest version on 2026-08-24, of which 24,220 were active and 257 deprecated. The registry gained 2,388 servers in the seven days since the previous sweep, against 28 that disappeared."
    },
    {
      "q": "Does the MCP registry verify that a server owns the repository it links to?",
      "a": "No. It verifies the namespace via GitHub OAuth or a DNS TXT record, but the repository URL is self-declared. The publishing token needs no repository scopes because the registry never reads your code."
    },
    {
      "q": "Does a namespace-repository mismatch mean the server is fraudulent?",
      "a": "No. Mismatch only means the namespace owner and the repository owner are different strings, and ownership transfers produce that difference honestly. It is a prompt to look at the specific entry, not a verdict — though the four in the top 100 are hard to read charitably."
    },
    {
      "q": "Why do MCP server rankings disagree with each other?",
      "a": "Most rank by GitHub stars taken from the repository field without checking whether that repository belongs to the publisher, and 22.2% of the registry declares no repository at all and drops out of every such ranking."
    },
    {
      "q": "How often is this ranking updated?",
      "a": "Every Monday. The full registry is swept, GitHub stars are re-joined, and the table plus the changelog are updated in place at the same URL. Week-over-week star deltas appear from the 2026-08-24 edition onward."
    }
  ],
